    "count": null,
    "comment": "Neurons whose footprints form two groups more than 4 px apart (smallest distance between the groups; >= 2 footprints each) that look like two cells: footprints overlap little across the groups but well within each group, which rejects single cells whose footprint shape changed. E.g. a cascaded mismatch from some session on, or alternating assignments of two cells. Sources: the group with the first detection, targets: the other group. Repair in the Footprints panel: right-click a highlighted footprint > 'Merge with selected neuron' > highlighted footprints, or 'Move highlighted footprints to…'.",
